# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Data — downloaded by scripts/fetch_data.py, never committed
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ANCHORED with a leading slash, deliberately. An unanchored "data/" matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth, which silently swallowed
# tests/data/fixedpoint_vectors.txt, the committed cross-language contract
# vectors. That file has to be in the repo or the boundary test cannot run on a
# fresh clone. Only the top-level MovieLens download is meant to be ignored.
/data/
model/out/
*.bin
!tests/**/*.bin
!tests/data/**

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Generated artefacts
#  Raw benchmark data (bench/results/*.jsonl) IS committed.
#  Figures are generated by `make figures` and are NOT.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bench/figures/

# Raw wire CAPTURES are not committed, though the benchmark ROWS beside them
# are. distinguisher.jsonl is 1.5 MB of base64 and transcript.jsonl 270 KB, and
# both are regenerated by `mingw32-make distinguisher` / `demo-net`. What a
# reader can actually check -- the analysis and its confidence intervals -- is
# in distinguisher_result.jsonl, which IS committed, alongside the script that
# produced it. Same reasoning as figures: keep what is checkable, regenerate
# what is bulk.
bench/results/distinguisher.jsonl
bench/results/transcript.jsonl
bench/results/transcript.*.jsonl
*.pdf
# Reference papers are linked from references/INDEX.md, not redistributed.
#
# The project's own documents are tracked, so anyone can read them without
# a LaTeX toolchain: the final report, the literature survey, the mid-term
# report and its technical companion, and the two presentation decks.
!report/final.pdf
!report/survey.pdf
!report/midterm_report.pdf
!report/midterm_technical.pdf
!report/slides/survey_slides.pdf
!report/slides/OblivRec_final_presentation.pdf
!report/slides/OblivRec_presentation_script.pdf

